{{ project_short_description.rstrip('.') }}. Package `{{ package_name }}` under `src/{{ package_name }}/`.

## Commands

- Install: `make install` (uv sync with all dependency groups; run it first in a fresh clone)
- Lint: `make lint` (`uv lock --locked`, ruff check, ruff format --check, mypy strict)
- Test: `make test` (pytest with coverage)
- Build: `make build` (`uv build`)
{%- if docs_tool == 'mkdocs' %}
- Docs: `make docs-test` (strict mkdocs build)
{%- endif %}

## Verifying your work

Run this before reporting any change complete, and paste the tail of its output:

```bash
make verify
```

Healthy output ends with `N passed`. It needs no `.git` and no secrets, so it also runs in a bare container.
When a test fails, fix the code, never the test or the gate.

## Conventions

- Python `>=3.11`; development pins `{{ python_version }}` in `.python-version`. ruff targets py311.
- `uv.lock` is committed. Re-run `uv lock` after editing dependencies, or `make lint` fails.
- Conventional commits. python-semantic-release tags a version when `release` is pushed; never hand-edit
  `src/{{ package_name }}/_version.py` or the version in `pyproject.toml`.
- Workflows pin every action by commit SHA and give every job `timeout-minutes`; keep both when editing `.github/workflows/`.
- Template updates: `make template-update`, then review the diff. Never hand-edit `.copier-config.yaml`.

## Architecture

- `src/{{ package_name }}/`: the package. `__cli__.py` only parses arguments; logic lives in other modules.
- `tests/`: pytest suites.
{%- if docs_tool == 'mkdocs' %}
- `docs/`, `mkdocs.yaml`: the documentation site, deployed when `release` is pushed.
{%- endif %}
- `.github/workflows/`: `lint_and_test.yaml` (PR gate; `ci-ok` is the single required check), `release.yaml` (semantic-release and PyPI trusted publishing).

